# Source NAT Pools

A source NAT pool allows traffic to use one or more explicitly defined translated addresses.

A pool may contain:

- One public IP
- Multiple public IPs
- A public address range

Conceptual example:

security {
    nat {
        source {
            pool INTERNET_POOL {
                address {
                    198.51.100.10/32;
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

This example uses documentation-only addressing.

